B.ceo=new A.CT("Great Wall of China","Beijing","China",40.4319,116.5704,"A series of walls and fortifications built along the northern border of China to protect Chinese states from invaders. Counting all of its offshoots, its length is more than 13,000 miles.","images/maps_great_wall_of_china.jpg","images/maps-great-wall-of-china.png")
B.cep=new A.CT("Petra","Ma'an Governorate","Jordan",30.3285,35.4444,"An ancient stone city located in southern Jordan. It became the capital city for the Nabataeans around the fourth century BC.","images/maps_petra.jpg","images/maps-petra.jpg")
B.ceq=new A.CT("Christ the Redeemer","Rio de Janeiro","Brazil",-22.9519,-43.2105,"An enormous statue of Jesus Christ with open arms, constructed between 1922 and 1931.","images/maps_christ_redeemer.jpg","images/maps-christ-the-redeemer.jpg")
B.cer=new A.CT("Taj Mahal","Uttar Pradesh","India",27.1751,78.0421,"A white marble mausoleum in Agra, India. It was commissioned in A.D. 1632 by the Mughal emperor Shah Jahan to hold the remains of his favorite wife. It was completed in 1653.","images/maps_taj_mahal.jpg","images/maps-tajmahal.jpg")
B.ces=new A.CT("Chichen Itza","Yucatan","Mexico",20.6843,-88.5678,"Mayan ruins on Mexico's Yucatan Peninsula. It was one of the largest Maya cities, thriving from around A.D. 600 to 1200.","images/maps_chichen_itza.jpg","images/maps-chichen-itza.jpg")
B.cet=new A.CT("Colosseum","Regio III Isis et Serapis","Rome",41.8902,12.4922,"Built between A.D. 70 and 80, it could accommodate 50,000 to 80,000 people in tiered seating. It is one of the most popular tourist attractions in Europe.","images/maps_colosseum.jpg","images/maps-colosseum.jpg")
B.ceu=new A.CT("Machu Picchu","Cuzco","Peru",-13.1631,-72.545,"An Inca citadel built in the mid-1400s. It was not widely known until the early twentieth century.","images/maps_machu_pichu.jpg","images/maps-machu-picchu.jpg")
